# Release signing credentials.
#
# !! This template is TRACKED BY GIT. Never put real values in this file. !!
#
# Copy it to `keystore.properties` in the project root and fill that in instead — that file is
# gitignored and is the one Gradle actually reads:
#
#   cp keystore.properties.template keystore.properties
#
# Then `./gradlew assembleRelease` produces a signed, installable APK at
# app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release.apk
#
# Without keystore.properties the release build still succeeds, but comes out unsigned and
# cannot be installed on a device.
#
# Use the same keystore you signed earlier releases with. Signing with a different key means
# Android treats it as a different app and refuses to install over the existing one.
#
# CI can supply these as environment variables instead:
#   ZENDRIVE_STORE_FILE, ZENDRIVE_STORE_PASSWORD, ZENDRIVE_KEY_ALIAS, ZENDRIVE_KEY_PASSWORD

# Absolute path to the .jks / .keystore file. On Windows use forward slashes:
#   C:/Users/you/keys/zendrive.jks
storeFile=

storePassword=
keyAlias=
keyPassword=
